# Only `out/` (compiled JS + the vendored grammar wasm) and the two real
# runtime `dependencies` (see package.json) need to ship in the .vsix.
# Everything else here is source, dev tooling, or test-only.

.vscode-test.mjs
.vscode/**
.github/**
.gitignore
eslint.config.mjs
tsconfig.json
vitest.config.mts
scripts/**
src/**
out/test/**
out/**/*.map
package-lock.json
*.vsix

# web-tree-sitter ships a second full copy of its wasm/js under debug/ for
# an explicit `web-tree-sitter/debug` import subpath we never use (we always
# get the production build via the default `require("web-tree-sitter")`
# resolution) -- and source maps for a bundled library aren't useful in an
# installed extension. Together these roughly halve the packaged size.
node_modules/web-tree-sitter/debug/**
node_modules/**/*.map

